<<<
The pronunciation of long u (as i, or 00) is a point that has been discussed at length for the special case in which practical doubts arise, i.e. when | precedes the u; see LU.
===
The pronunciation of long u (as ū, or o͞o) is a point that has been discussed at length for the special case in which practical doubts arise, i. e. when l precedes the u; see ^^LU^^.
>>>

<<<
1. When it is the other liquid, r, attempts at ū are difficult; few people make them, & 00 (or 00) being generally accepted should be made universal (see PRONUNCIATION); so rool (rule), kro6d (crude), introo’zhn (intrusion), kwé’roolus & ga’rddlus (querulous, garrulous), groo (grew), froot (fruit).
===
1. When it is the other liquid, r, attempts at ū are difficult; few people make them, & o͞o (or o͝o) being generally accepted should be made universal (see ^^PRONUNCIATION^^); so ro͞ol (*rule*), kro͞od (*crude*), intro͞o'zhn (*intrusion*), kwĕ'ro͝o*lus* & gă'ro͝ol*us* (*querulous, garrulous*), gro͞o (*grew*), fro͞ot (*fruit*).
>>>

<<<
2. When no letter precedes, U is invariable (unit, ubiquity, &c.) except in foreign words such as uhlan, Ural, unberufen, umlaut.
===
2. When no letter precedes, ū is invariable (*unit, ubiquity*, &c.) except in foreign words such as *uhlan, Ural, unberufen, umlaut*.
>>>

<<<
3. After the sounds ch, j, sh, zh, attempts at ū are as ill advised as after r; so ch0d0, joon, jO0t, jos, shoot, shoor, a’zhooal, for chew, June, jute, juice, chute, sure, usual; not chi, jūn, jūt, jūs, shit, shir,
===
3. After the sounds ch, j, sh, zh, attempts at ū are as ill advised as after r; so cho͞o, jo͞on, jo͞ot, jo͞os, sho͞ot, shoor, ū'zho͝o*al*, for *chew, June, jute, juice, chute, sure, usual*; not chū, jūn, jūt, jūs, shūt, shūr,
>>>

<<<
typographie(al). Both forms
===
**typographic(al).** Both forms
>>>
